#
# The switch's queues a plugin asked for - its TCAM entries on port 0, the ports' scheduling, the
# chip's weights and with them port 0's pause off, egress limits - set again at every boot:
# scripts/xgs/switch_qos.py.
#
# The coprocessor's boot erases the switch's registers, and the host's boot boots the coprocessor. So
# when a plugin has left its settings file, they are set again here, once the boot is done; detached,
# because the script waits for the coprocessor's link to be given its address and for the switch's
# frame limit (09-xgs-switch-jumbo) first, and a boot must not wait for either. With no settings file
# - the plugin switched off or removed - and a state that still holds what a put-back could not finish,
# only that is put back: nothing is set. Nothing to do without either. The script logs what it did (tag
# xgs-switch) and never fails the boot.
SCRIPT=/usr/local/opnsense/scripts/xgs/switch_qos.py
[ -f "${SCRIPT}" ] || exit 0
[ -f /var/db/os-xgs-npu/switch-qos.json ] || [ -f /var/db/os-xgs-npu/switch-qos.state ] || exit 0
/usr/sbin/daemon -f /usr/local/bin/python3 "${SCRIPT}" reapply --boot
exit 0
